PARITY — web VehicleHeader.tsx reproduced VERBATIM (covenant #5)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Web source is a pure presentational `GlassPanel` masthead taking { vehicle?, status, onWake, waking }:
  • back `<Link to="/vehicles"><ArrowLeft/></Link>`        -> VehicleHeaderBackButton (onBack closure)
  • status `<Badge variant={statusVariant(status)} dot size="lg">{status}</Badge>`
                                                           -> VehicleHeaderStatusPill (dot + tone tint + label)
  • model `<Badge variant="neutral" size="sm">{model} {trim_badging}</Badge>`
                                                           -> VehicleHeaderModelChip ("model trim", verbatim)
  • VIN  `<p class="… truncate font-mono">{vin}</p>`       -> mono VIN row, lineLimit(1) .tail
  • Wake `<Button onClick loading={waking} icon={<Power/>}>t('common.wakeUp','Wake Up')</Button>`
                                                           -> VehicleHeaderWakeButton (TSButton primary,
                                                              isLoading: waking, SF Symbol "power")

statusVariant() ported VERBATIM from web @/types/fsm VEHICLE_STATE_ENTRIES (VehicleHeaderProjector.variant):
  online->success  driving->success  charging->warning  parked->info  updating->info
  asleep->neutral  offline->danger   unknown->danger  (the web `?? 'danger'` safety branch)
Model/trim chip text = [model, trim_badging] trimmed, blank parts dropped, joined " " (web `{model} {trim}`),
nil when both blank (web renders a lone space; native shows no empty chip). VIN trimmed, nil when blank.
VehicleStatusKind(raw:) mirrors deriveVehicleStatus(null)->offline + unrecognized->unknown.

